WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.100
How does build-heap work? Repair

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.680
internal nodes from the bottom

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.220
upwards, so every heapify call

4
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.360
starts with valid child subtrees.

5
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.260
This builds a heap in

6
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.160
linear time, which is more

7
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.060
subtle than it looks.

8
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.400
Start with seven, six, five,

9
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.233
four, three, two, one in

10
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.400
zero-based array order. The last

11
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.260
internal index is floor of

12
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.300
n over two, minus one;

13
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.600
here that is index two.

14
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.940
Indices three through six are

15
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.900
leaves, and each leaf is

16
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.340
already a valid heap. Process

17
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.440
internal indices two, one, then

18
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.640
zero, which puts every child

19
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.860
before its parent in the

20
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:42.640
repair schedule.

21
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.800
At index two, five has

22
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.260
children two and one. Swap

23
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.920
five with the smaller child,

24
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.300
one, and that subtree is

25
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:52.640
repaired.

26
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.260
At index one, six has

27
00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.560
children four and three. Swap

28
00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.760
six with three, so the

29
00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.760
second child subtree is also

30
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.140
a min-heap.

31
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.540
Now repair the root seven:

32
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.300
choose child one, and swap.

33
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.980
Continue down with seven, choose

34
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.240
child two, and swap again;

35
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.820
now the entire array satisfies

36
00:01:15.379 --> 00:01:16.040
min-heap order.

37
00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.580
The array is one, three,

38
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.780
two, four, six, seven, five.

39
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.040
Every parent is no larger

40
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.720
than its children, but the

41
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.280
array is not fully sorted.

42
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.500
A heap exposes the minimum

43
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.100
without ordering every pair.

44
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.340
Multiplying n heapify calls by

45
00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.740
the root cost log n

46
00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.560
gives an upper bound, but

47
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.760
it is loose. Most nodes

48
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.360
are near the bottom, so

49
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.680
most cannot travel down logarithmically

50
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.320
many levels.

51
00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.540
At height h, there are

52
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.200
at most order n over

53
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.700
two to the power h

54
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.200
plus one nodes. Charge each

55
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.240
order h work; the weighted

56
00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.000
geometric sum is a constant

57
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:55.900
times n.

58
00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.020
The loop processes linearly many

59
00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.760
internal nodes, supplying a matching

60
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.480
linear lower bound for this

61
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.020
implementation. Bottom-up build-heap therefore takes

62
00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.020
theta n time, while repeated

63
00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.860
insertion has an n log

64
00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.540
n worst-case bound.

65
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.480
Things to take note of.

66
00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.120
Use iterative heapify for constant

67
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.860
auxiliary space, and include recursive

68
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.620
frames if you implement repair

69
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.700
recursively. Empty and singleton arrays

70
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.260
have no internal node to

71
00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:26.680
process.

72
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.280
Do not scan internal nodes

73
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.000
from the root down: the

74
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.780
required child heaps may not

75
00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.540
exist yet. Linear heap construction

76
00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.700
does not imply linear comparison

77
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.100
sorting, because the resulting heap

78
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.700
is only partially ordered. Quite

79
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.900
a useful distinction.
